{
  "name": "ISMC part of London's Knowledge Quarter",
  "parent_id": 203314133681389,
  "group_id": "d097843d-2af5-448c-a8e2-67f86c99e371",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:19:30.468Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-07-31T09:19:30.549Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-31T09:19:30.536Z",
  "id": 203980679076907,
  "uuid": "6cbeb343-2555-4bcb-8247-b24bb00c67b2",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "b78c8bac-c0a1-b952-265c-037e074e535a",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "690e07b7-468a-75de-437e-72598530cd3f",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The members, which range from the British Library itself, the British Museum, University College London (UCL) and the University of the Arts to the Digital Catapult, the Wellcome Trust and the Guardian, in addition to ISMC, will work together to share information, ideas, research and innovation. The aim of the Knowledge Quarter is to make the outstanding facilities, collections and expertise of its members understood, available and used as widely as possible for the benefit of researchers, creative people, students and the local community.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "As well as established organisations, the Knowledge Quarter includes The Francis Crick Institute, now under construction, which will be a leading global centre for medical research, and Google, which is to build its new UK headquarters in King's Cross.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Clustered around King's Cross, the Euston Road and Bloomsbury is an incredible range of knowledge resources and expertise, ranging from the world's earliest books and manuscripts to the latest fashion and creative designs and cutting-edge medical research.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Together, members of the Knowledge Quarter employ over 30,000 people, turn over more than £2bn, work with 3,500 volunteers, and serve more than 8m visitors annually. The Knowledge Quarter is governed by a Board and a steering group, on which all partner organisations are represented",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Deputy London Mayor for Business & Enterprise, Kit Malthouse said: \"London leads the way in supporting the UK's knowledge economy.  I am proud that within our great capital city we have leading international organisations that are coming together, through the Knowledge Quarter, to find ways that they can support growth and innovation through research.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Commenting on the initiative, Dr David Taylor, Director, Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations said: \"Belonging to the Knowledge Quarter consortium is an excellent way for the Institute to benefit from its location in the centre of London, and to share its research and insights more broadly.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
